ead off out of nowhere and that reminds  me right he's a dick but it also makes  me go Leyna he's a dick but he must have  some sort of plan if he did that and as  a result I think it would be very  difficult to ask for a better antihero  style presence to follow but as for the  character who I suppose acts as the  protagonist we have Thor Finn and I'm  similarly invested in him not quite to  the same degree though big or small I am  completely on board with his quest for  revenge I think it has made him a bit  OneNote so far he's very much the polar  opposite of a Scot because I feel like I  always know what Thorin is thinking and  feeling which i think is an intentional  juxtaposition that results in making  Thoth in less mysterious however it does  make him very easy to empathize with and  use as a vehicle for the audience's  journey  so even when Thor Fionn is doing  horrific things it's still very easy to  be on board with him as well as quite  painful when we do see him suffer which  is you know pretty much his entire  existence in villain saga however I do  remember one particular moment at the  end of the episode where he fought  thorkil where he was just completely  broken and trudging along the road but  this wash of misery all over his face it  was such a well-done moment and it's one  of those scenes that makes me double  down on my support for this kid and I'm  really interested to see if his journey  concludes with the revenge he lost after  so much well whether he will adopt his  father's words that nobody is his enemy  and finally start living a life for  himself speaking of his father  Thor's was quite the character even if  you discount the opening which made his  future death pretty clear he was death  flagged quite heavily because you soon  enough realized that nobody this good  can survive in a world like this I did  really liked the idea that one day on  the battlefield he just  feeling empty and decided you know what  no more of this because s