ed in and I get that the Thor fin  stuff would have been really difficult  if not completely impossible to keep out  of the opening because his adolescent  form makes up the bulk of the series or  at least that's what I'm assuming but at  the same time there were a good what  five episodes before he actually grew to  the point that the opening showed him in  that's quite a bit of time to keep  plodding along with near exact knowledge  of what's to come and hey it's not a big  issue because Finland soccer is just so  damn good but I just prefer to go into  things a bit more blind than that and  the standard response I'm going to get  this is well just don't watch the  openings lull which is great but that  doesn't do me a whole lot of good after  I've already seen it the first time and  made all of those connections whatever  the case it does not matter because the  journey is worth taking even if the  destination is known beforehand look  Finland saga is an undeniable shard of  glory in this anime season if it keeps  going the way it has and I have no  reason to believe that it won't and I  think it's a solid contender for the  best series of 2019 and for good reason  it's fantastically animated well paced  wonderfully performed and a never  intriguingly written piece of media I  find it so difficult to point out flaws  with this series but the best I can  offer is the slight annoyance at  spoilers in the opening and that should  tell you what a nifty series this is  because I am very capable of criticizing  the hell out of anything but it's also  refreshing because Finland saga doesn't  take place in Japan or any place based  on Japan in fact there are some points  in the series where I actually forget  that they're speaking Japanese that's  how immersed I became in this and just  quickly that's another thing actually I  really like how they treat language in  the show I mean everyone is obviously  speaking Japanese for the sake of the  audience but there is constant reference  to not understanding what someone else  is saying  because they're speaking Norse English  or Welsh whatever and it adds a nice  layer of realistic complexity to the  situation at hand rather than everyone  being able to magically understand each  other and it does so without having  actors actually trying to speak those  languages although to be perfectly  honest I would love to see the Japanese  attempt to speak Welsh because it's kind  of like the anti-japanese actually  because their words have so few vowels  and Japanese is all about vowel sounds  but finally the thing that sold me most  initially on Finland saga is that it  began in Iceland so it activated all  kinds of nostalgia for me because  Iceland is one of the most beautiful  countries I've ever been to expensive as  hell but it's like stepping into another  world entirely and I think that the  anime really captured that magical  aspect of Iceland quite nicely by the  way if you're of a keen for a magical  story about Iceland and look up that one  time that one of their construction  companies was forced to unearth an elf  rock because elves started causing a  series of mishaps with their machinery  and no I am NOT jerking elves are a very  established presence in Iceland but to  bring this back around  I love Finland saga great series so far  and I look forward to tuning in for the  next 11 or so weeks to see it continue  but that pretty much does it for my  first impressions of Finland sorry if  you enjoyed this video and the content  this channel produced in general and  please do consider donating to the new  worldview patreon because the support of  all of your amazing people is what  continues to make this channel possible  and if patreon isn't quite your style  then please do leave this video a like  share or subscribe because it also helps  support this channel an incredible  amount and if you'd like to join the fun  at any time then please do head over to  my desk or server where 